An EEG Dataset of Overt and Covert Speech Recorded with Tripolar Concentric Ring Electrodes
============================================================================================

Overview
--------
EEG from 16 adult participants recorded with tripolar concentric ring electrodes (TCRE) while they
named pictures aloud (overt speech) or silently (covert speech). Every TCRE provides two co-located
signals: a tripolar signal (an estimate of the surface Laplacian) and an emulated conventional disc
signal (recorded from the outer ring). The dataset therefore allows a direct comparison of Laplacian
and conventional EEG recorded at the same scalp positions.

Participants
------------
16 adults (sub-01 to sub-16). participants.tsv lists gender, handedness,
language background, TCRE size (4 or 10 mm outer diameter), electrodes per array, EOG channels
and run order. Participants are identified only by their BIDS labels.

Task
----
4 runs of 50 trials per participant (200 trials), one condition per run: 2 overt runs and 2 covert
runs; the run order differs between participants (participants.tsv, run_order).
Each trial: a picture shown for 3.5 s, during which the participant named it aloud (overt) or
silently (covert), followed by a 2.5 s grey screen (rest).
Events: one marker at each picture onset, labelled Stimulus/Overt or Stimulus/Covert
(events.tsv). The grey screen began 3.5 s after each marker; it has no marker of its own.

Recording
---------
BrainAmp amplifier and BrainVision Recorder (Brain Products GmbH). Reference and ground on the right
mastoid. Sampling rate 1000 Hz (sub-01) or 2500 Hz (all others); resolution 0.1 uV.
Hardware filters: high-pass 10 s time constant (0.016 Hz); low-pass 1000 Hz (40/42-channel recordings)
or 250 Hz (56/64-channel recordings). No notch or software filter during recording.
Power-line frequency 60 Hz.

Channels
--------
TCRE k is recorded on channels 2k-1 and 2k:
  odd channel  (2k-1) = tripolar (TCRE Laplacian) signal
  even channel (2k)   = emulated disc signal of the same electrode
The channel names are placeholder labels from the recording software; they do NOT give the
electrode positions. Positions are given by the array layout below.

The electrodes form four arrays centred on F4, P6, F3 and P5 (10-10 system). Channels are ordered
by array (F4, P6, F3, P5) and, within an array, from the lowest (most inferior) electrode upward.

  Participants                       Electrodes per array   Array channels   EOG channels
                                     (F4/P6/F3/P5)
  sub-01                             5/5/5/5                1-40             none
  sub-07, 08, 09, 14, 15, 16         5/5/5/5                1-40             41-42
  sub-05, 06                         7/7/7/7                1-56             none
  sub-02, 03, 04, 10                 8/8/8/8                1-64             none
  sub-11, 12, 13                     8/7/8/8                1-62             63-64

EOG channels: two standard disc electrodes (not TCREs), placed above and to the right of one eye,
recorded as the last two channels. They are labelled EOG in channels.tsv, so
mne_bids.read_raw_bids loads them as EOG and picks="eeg" excludes them.

Code
----
code/make_cleaned_epochs.py (with code/channel_sets.py) generates derivatives/cleaned-epochs and
code/make_resampled.py generates derivatives/resampled-500hz from the raw data.
code/artifact_ica_ssp.py applies optional ICA or SSP artifact removal to the resampled recordings,
separately for the TCRE and disc signals. The analysis code of the data descriptor is available at
https://github.com/parasmemon/tcre-overt-covert-speech-eeg

Derivatives
-----------
derivatives/cleaned-epochs: epoched, cleaned recordings generated by code/make_cleaned_epochs.py
(MNE .fif).

derivatives/resampled-500hz: continuous recordings of all channels, including EOG, resampled to
500 Hz (MNE .fif, polyphase resampling with anti-aliasing filter). No notch or band-pass filter
and no rejection. See derivatives/resampled-500hz/README.


Loading
-------
  from mne_bids import BIDSPath, read_raw_bids
  raw = read_raw_bids(BIDSPath(subject="01", task="OvertCovert", datatype="eeg", root="."))
  import mne
  epochs = mne.read_epochs("derivatives/cleaned-epochs/sub-01/eeg/sub-01_task-OvertCovert_desc-cleaned_epo.fif")


Notes
-----
- Absolute amplitudes differ between tripolar and disc signals; compare them with relative
  (scale-free) measures such as relative band power, percentage change or correlation.
- Each run contains only one condition, so overt/covert comparisons are also comparisons between runs.
- Participants often began naming soon after picture onset; speech-related muscle activity is
  present in overt trials.

